From 8dce5c84553cbb28d83a290fa50b4740f0c8eeeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Data-crea <sattler.daniel@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:23:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Extension API: src/ext and its hooks in the engine
 (OrionLayer local)

The TCP Extension API OrionLayer talks to on localhost:17362, as it
stands in Data's working tree on 17 September 2026: src/ext/ (ext_api,
ext_server), the ORION2RE_EXT option in CMakeLists.txt, ext::Tick and
the pending-field early exit in fields::Get_Input_, ext::Init/Tick/
Shutdown in mox2.cpp, and the hidden-window guard in platform.cpp.

src/ext/ was never tracked, so the fixes that live inside it cannot be
separated into commits of their own without inventing intermediate
states that were never built. This commit therefore also carries the
src/ext parts of these items from OrionLayer's doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md:
open fix 1 (SendFrame retry), 2 (FIELD_LIST after HELLO), 3 (INJECT_CLICK
coordinate half), 12 (MSG_SET_JOBS), 14 (MSG_SAVE_SLOTS), 20 (fleet
selection, revision 2) and 21 (MSG_SELECT_SHIP). Their hunks in tracked
engine files follow as separate commits.

Committed as found: no byte of the working tree changed (OrionLayer
work order 126, part A).

Ported onto orion2re v2.0.0 in scratch (work order 242 e) from local a111355d:
renamed 3-way merge (identifier map cf4d9617->v2.0.0); by hand: platform.cpp guard re-placed on v2's SDL_ShowWindow (v2 reworked window/renderer creation); CMake block moved out of if(TARGET orion2re) and onto orion2re_game_objects (v2 compiles the game sources in that object library).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
